From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:36:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Support multiple LLM providers for the classifier

Adds providers.py, a small dispatch layer so classifier.py isn't tied
to Anthropic: LLM_PROVIDER in .env now selects Anthropic, OpenAI, Grok
(xAI) or Gemini, each with its own key variable and default model,
overridable via LLM_MODEL. OpenAI, Grok and Gemini share the openai
SDK pointed at different base_urls since Grok and Gemini both publish
OpenAI-compatible endpoints; Anthropic keeps its own SDK path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
